item.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;hs-featured-image-wrapper&quot;&gt; 
 &lt;a class=&quot;hs-featured-image-link&quot; href=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/pci-ssc-celebrates-world-standards-day-and-20-years-of-securing-payment-data&quot; title=&quot;&quot;&gt; &lt;img alt=&quot;PCI SSC Celebrates World Standards Day and 20 Years of Securing Payment Data&quot; class=&quot;hs-featured-image&quot; src=&quot;https://blog.pcisecuritystandards.org/hubfs/2026-blog/standards-blog.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width: auto !important; float: left; margin: 0 15px 15px 0;&quot; /&gt; &lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;/div&gt; 
&lt;br /&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Every year on 14 October, &lt;span style=&quot;color: #0a5d66;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.worldstandardsday.org/home.html&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold; color: #0a5d66;&quot;&gt;World Standards Day&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; recognizes the people and organizations working together to develop standards that make our world safer, more connected, and more resilient. For the PCI Security Standards Council, this year’s celebration carries special significance: for 20 years, we have been setting payment &lt;span style=&quot;color: #0a5d66;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/standards/&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold; color: #0a5d66;&quot;&gt;security standards&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; that help protect payment data around the globe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a current list of where and when I am scheduled to speak:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I’m speaking at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.attentionconferences.com/conferences/2026-forum&quot;&gt;ATTENTION: Democracy, Rebuilt&lt;/a&gt; in Montreal, Quebec, Canada. The event runs October 21–23, 2026, and my talk is on Wednesday, October 21.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I’m speaking at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/conversations-in-computing-bruce-schneier-on-hacking-ai-tickets-1998780074007&quot;&gt;University of Toronto&lt;/a&gt; in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, at 5 PM ET on October 22, 2026.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I’m speaking at &lt;a href=&quot;https://unpromptedcon.org/&quot;&gt;[un]prompted&lt;/a&gt; in San Francisco, California. The event runs October 27–29, 2026, and my talk is at 11:35 AM PT on Thursday, October 29.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I’m speaking at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://luma.com/a3pk9zbg&quot;&gt;Catalyst Summit&lt;/a&gt; in Brampton, Ontario, Canada, on Wednesday, November 18, 2026...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another IoT &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crq5nzxv9q4yo&quot;&gt;cyberattack&lt;/a&gt;, this one in France:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hackers gained control of the software that regulates the temperatures of the refrigeration units, forcing some to warm to 50C (120F) overnight, according to one supermarket chain affected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[&amp;#8230;]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Normally, supermarket freezers go through a short period of defrosting overnight, in which temperatures rise slightly. But the hackers ordered the units to heat up and stay hot, although Danfoss did not confirm any reports about just how warm the fridges and freezers could become in that process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Danfoss said the affected cold units were older models whose security software could not be updated to ward off a risk they had identified...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
